    <section class="kid-tale" aria-labelledby="kid-tale-title">
      <h2 class="kid-tale-title" id="kid-tale-title">The story of Aboriginal Australians</h2>
      <ol class="kid-tale-pages"><li class="kid-tale-np"><p>The ancestors of Aboriginal Australians arrived in Australia more than 50,000 years ago.</p><p>Back then Australia was joined to New Guinea by land, but they still had to cross the sea.</p></li><li><figure><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aboriginal-tasmanians.jpg" alt="Aboriginal Tasmanians" loading="lazy" width="320" height="220"><figcaption>Aboriginal Tasmanians <span class="kid-tale-cr">Benjamin Duterrau (1768–1851), Public domain</span></figcaption></figure><p>Over time they became hundreds of peoples, each with its own language and its own land, called Country.</p><p>They pass down stories of creation, called the Dreaming, through dance, songs, stories and art.</p></li><li class="kid-tale-np"><p>About 4,000 years ago their stone tools grew smaller, and new languages spread across the land.</p><p>Aboriginal peoples traded goods with each other across the whole continent.</p></li><li><figure><img src="/images/encyclopedia/makassan-contact-with-australia.jpg" alt="Makassan contact with Australia" loading="lazy" width="320" height="220"><figcaption>Makassan contact with Australia <span class="kid-tale-cr">Unknown author, Public domain</span></figcaption></figure><p>More than 350 years ago, fishers from Indonesia sailed to the north coast and brought dugout canoes.</p><p>From 1788 settlers from Britain took the land, and disease and fighting killed many Aboriginal people, who fought back.</p></li><li><figure><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kevin-rudd.jpg" alt="Kevin Rudd" loading="lazy" width="320" height="220"><figcaption>Kevin Rudd <span class="kid-tale-cr">Department of Foreign Affairs and Trade, CC BY 4.0</span></figcaption></figure><p>Many Aboriginal children were taken from their families, and in 2008 Prime Minister Kevin Rudd said sorry for this.</p><p>Today Aboriginal people have won back many rights, and they own or share about half of Australia's land.</p></li></ol>
    </section>

    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The ancestors of Aboriginal Australians reached Sahul, the land that joined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-guinea">New Guinea</a>, 50,000 to 65,000 years ago, and may have settled across the continent within 6,000 years of landing.</li><li>More than 400 distinct peoples, each with its own language and Country, pass down their beliefs through dance, stories, songlines and art, which together tell of creation in the Dreaming.</li><li>From 1788 British colonisation brought disease, frontier war and dispossession: in the 150 years that followed, 90% of Indigenous Australians died, and between 1910 and 1970 between 10 and 33 percent of Aboriginal children were removed from their families.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>A 2011 study of DNA from an early-20th-century lock of an Aboriginal person’s hair found that, outside <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>, Aboriginal peoples have lived continuously in the same territory longer than any other human population.</p></aside>
    </section>

